Overlay patch 0066 (D-085): SPIKE ATTRIBUTION PROBE + depth-kernel pipeline cache.

WHY. Round 1 (0065) proved the tick catch-up on the user's iPhone Air: tps
19.99-20.06 in every window, music right. What is left is the fps dips
themselves: in bad windows SOH_PACE busy_ms p95 = 8.5-10.9 ms (max 17-58 ms)
against ~3 ms in good windows, with the GPU idle and thermal 0. SOH_PACE can
say THAT the game thread is busy, not WITH WHAT. This probe answers that.

WHAT IT MEASURES. Every 2D engine frame is cut at the 0065 pace seams
(drawable acquired / LUS sleep begins) plus three marks inside
Fast3dWindow::DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands, and the record closes in
Fast3dWindow right after Interpreter::EndFrame (post-sleep):

  gap    previous frame's post-sleep -> this frame's drawable request.
         Holds the game tick on the first frame of each tick (logic), the
         audio hand-off wait (aud), SDL_PumpEvents = every UIKit main-thread
         callback (ev), FrameInterpolation_Interpolate (interp).
  wait   nextDrawable (0065).
  busy   drawable -> LUS sleep (0065), split into
           menu  ImGui NewFrame + DrawMenu + CalculateGameViewport
           run   Interpreter::StartFrame + Run (the display list)
           gui   Gui::EndDraw (DrawGame, ImGui render, floating windows)
           end   GfxRenderingAPIMetal::EndFrame (mips, commit, present)
  cpu    gap + busy. A frame whose cpu exceeds the frame period
         (1000 / interpolation fps: 8.33 ms at 120) is a SPIKE.

Seam categories (overlapping the split; game thread = the main thread on
iOS, pthread_main_np):
   0 res    resource cache MISS loaded on the game thread (archive read +
            decompress + parse), n / ms / bytes, and the 3 largest by name
   1 rd     the archive read + decompress part of res
   2 bg     cache misses loaded on the resource pool threads (LoadResource
            is LoadResourceAsync().get(): the game thread waits for them)
   3 rwait  ResourceManager::LoadResource on the game thread (hits + waits)
   4 tex    Interpreter::ImportTexture (decode + upload of a new texture)
   5 up     Metal texture uploads, n / bytes (from 0019's ledger; their ms
            is inside tex)
   6 shd    CreateAndLoadNewShader on the game thread (compile is async)
   7 zdep   GfxRenderingAPIMetal::GetPixelDepth: a compute dispatch that
            COMMITS AND waitUntilCompleted()s on the game thread. Called by
            Environment_GraphCallback (sun lens flare + light glows) once
            per game tick in every Play scene.
   8 zpso   the newComputePipelineState it creates on EVERY call (upstream)

THE ONE FIX IN THIS PATCH (gSohIos.DepthPsoCache, default 1): the depth
kernel's compute pipeline is built once and reused instead of per call. No
fidelity change (same kernel, same values). Proven by this probe on the
simulator: zpso 0.18-0.3 ms per tick, and one call took 21.8 ms (a 23 ms
spike, all of it zpso). The bigger part of zdep -- the commit +
waitUntilCompleted GPU drain -- is NOT changed here; see D-085 for the plan.
   9 fbrd   ReadFramebufferToCPU (waits on the GPU too)
  10 actor  Actor_Spawn       11 obj  Object_Spawn   12 room  room resource load
  13 cvsave ConsoleVariables::Save (CVarSave and the Gui's deferred save)
  14 aud    Graph_ProcessGfxCommands waiting on the audio thread
  15 ev     wnd->HandleEvents (SDL pump: touches, timers, the 0.25 s poll)
  16 interp FrameInterpolation_Interpolate
plus per-frame triangles / vertices / draw calls from the interpreter, so a
spike with more work can be told from a spike with the same work done slower
(a clock or core change).

OUTPUT.
  SOH_SPIKE  one line per spike frame, at most 20 per 10 s window (the rest
             are counted): the split, the content counters, every non-zero
             category as name=n/ms[/kb], and top=<path>:<ms>:<kb> for the
             largest loads (bg: prefix for pool-thread loads).
  SOH_SPKWIN one line per 10 s: frames, spikes, cpu p50/p95/max, per-frame
             average of each split over ALL frames / over SPIKE frames, each
             category's n / total ms / ms inside spike frames (+MB), and the
             content counters. Attribution works without a single spike line.

COST. Two mach_absolute_time reads and a pthread_main_np per seam event, a
handful of steady_clock reads per frame, no allocation in the hot path
(fixed arrays; names copied into fixed buffers). gSohIos.SpikeProbe (default
1) switches it off (re-read every 60 frames) for the probe-cost A/B: compare
SOH_PACE busy_ms p50 with it on and off.

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0065 applied and 0066 not applied.
Every hunk keeps clear of earlier patches' hunks and 3-line contexts so the
series stays reversible (apply-overlay.sh checks it on every run).


